## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to apply SWAR bit counting to 128-bit data without branches. Also checks splitting 128-bit into halves and combining results efficiently.

## Key Concepts
- SWAR bitcount technique for 64-bit words
- Handling 128-bit data via hi/lo halves
- Branchless arithmetic for performance

## Code Example
```javascript
unsigned int popcount64(uint64_t v) {
  v = v - ((v >> 1) & 0x5555555555555555);
  v = (v & 0x3333333333333333) + ((v >> 2) & 0x3333333333333333);
  v = (v + (v >> 4)) & 0x0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f;
  return (v * 0x0101010101010101) >> 56;
}
```
Then: hiCount = popcount64(x.hi); loCount = popcount64(x.lo); return hiCount + loCount;

